#=GF RT   Cloning and sequencing of the gene encoding the spike protein of
#=GF RT   the coronavirus IBV.
#=GF RA   Binns MM, Boursnell ME, Cavanagh D, Pappin DJ, Brown TD;
#=GF RL   J Gen Virol 1985;66:719-726.
#=GF RN   [2]
#=GF RM   32150576
#=GF RT   Structure of mouse coronavirus spike protein complexed with
#=GF RT   receptor reveals mechanism for viral entry.
#=GF RA   Shang J, Wan Y, Liu C, Yount B, Gully K, Yang Y, Auerbach A,
#=GF RA   Peng G, Baric R, Li F;
#=GF RL   PLoS Pathog. 2020;16:e1008392.
#=GF RN   [3]
#=GF RM   26206723
#=GF RT   Bat-to-human: spike features determining 'host jump' of
#=GF RT   coronaviruses SARS-CoV, MERS-CoV, and beyond.
#=GF RA   Lu G, Wang Q, Gao GF;
#=GF RL   Trends Microbiol. 2015;23:468-478.
#=GF DR   INTERPRO; IPR002552;
#=GF DR   SO; 0100021; polypeptide_conserved_region;
#=GF CC   The coronavirus spike glycoprotein forms the characteristic
#=GF CC   'corona' after which the group is named. The Spike glycoprotein
#=GF CC   is translated as a large polypeptide that is subsequently
#=GF CC   cleaved to S1 Pfam:PF01600 and S2 [1], [2]. The S2 subunit
#=GF CC   normally contains multiple key components, including one or more
#=GF CC   fusion peptides (FP), a second proteolytic site (S2') and two
#=GF CC   conserved heptad repeats (HRs), driving membrane penetration and
#=GF CC   virus-cell fusion. The HRs can trimerize into a coiled-coil
#=GF CC   structure built of three HR1-HR2 helical hairpins presenting as
#=GF CC   a canonical six-helix bundle and drag the virus envelope and the
#=GF CC   host cell bilayer into close proximity, preparing for fusion to
#=GF CC   occur [3].
#=GF SQ   22
